{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition","id":1283793,"title":"Estimated date for 5th edition...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-30T14:03:10-08:00","id":1283793,"title":"Estimated date for 5th edition...","content":"I know that I am probably really jumping the gun, but after seeing, and loving, Vampire 5th edition, I would love to see Werewolf get the same treatment. Assuming that it IS coming out, any idea as to when we should see it released?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T15:46:40-08:00","id":1283810,"title":"","content":"2021 seeing as we've seen nothing about w5 except its coming and a Get of Fenris in one of the v5 alphas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T05:12:59-08:00","id":1283893,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> Wait a minute tell me what you know about this Fenrir Alpha Jarl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T15:07:52-08:00","id":1284014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition?p=1283893#post1283893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> Wait a minute tell me what you know about this Fenrir Alpha Jarl.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ....in one of the Alpha tests for v5 there was a &quot;IF you leave the city by cutting through the woods a Get of Fenris from the local sept attacks you&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T05:29:30-08:00","id":1284110,"title":"","content":"My bet is that once Paradox's restructuring of White Wolf is complete, they will begin the process of creating W5 (with some of that already having been done during their V5 work, as Rage as a mechanic was hinted at in the Animalism disciplines of the v5 corebook). The worldofdarkness.com website's update completion will be a good signpost of this progress I think (hasn't happened yet though to be clear). Much as I'd like it earlier as well, a playtest period of a year seems like what happened for V5, so 2021 sounds like a good estimate, factoring time to get corebook art commissioned and completed. My hope is for the website to be finished by mid-March, allowing most of 2019 for dev and writer team gathering and alpha testing, making 2020 a possibility. I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1107_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1107\" data-vbnamecard=\"1107\">maryshelly</a> - I love v5 and can't wait to see w5 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12074,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","user":"Robert D","date":". 02-01-2019, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T05:46:51-08:00","id":1284112,"title":"","content":"I dug out the pre-alpha v5 pdf from my files and here's the info it gives on the a Lupine Tracker NPC enemy. This was the pre-alpha, so the mechanics do not fully reflect the v5 corebook, but it's still an interesting point of speculation and study<br /> &quot;This is the weirdest one. If the coterie just sneaks into the wild to walk to a smaller town past the<br /> lockdown and steal a car there, they encounter -something- hunting for them. It\u2019s a Get of Fenris<br /> Lupine from the Grunewald Sept. They can run, but the wolf never loses their scent.<br /> <br /> Lupine Tracker<br /> Mental 2 Physical 5 Social 2<br /> Alertness 2 Combat 5 Other 1<br /> Potence 3 Fortitude 3 Rage 8<br /> Willpower 3 Health 9 Composure 1<br /> <br /> The Lupine tracker can spend Rage to gain extra actions (up to two extra per round) and<br /> regenerates one point of Superficial damage each turn. It does not suffer wound penalties and its<br /> claws and bite deal aggravated damage. Good luck! THE END&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, the v5 core also gave a werewolf NPC antagonist near the back of the book, which had the same regeneration rules, but no Rage value assigned in that NPC's block, though the NPC had high levels of Disciplines (for ease of using the NPC prior to W5's creation, bless the writer's hearts) to emulate gifts (I recall the V20, W20 and M20 books doing much the same thing), though since Hunger is risked for higher ranked disciplines, I imagine that as of the corebook's writing the Rage mechanic, like Hunger may be risked to perform certain supernatural feats, and if it rises too fill the Lupine to bursting with Rage, that's when things get Crinos rampage messy. The NPC stats also had some shapeshifting mechanics for Crinos form it seems. No sign in either the pre-alpha or the final V5 of Werewolf Gnosis or specific info or hints on how Breeds, Auspices, Gifts or Tribes work, though I imagine, as in times past, the Tribe will be the equivalent of Clan in terms of mechanical and story significance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12074,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","user":"Robert D","date":". 02-01-2019, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T10:58:29-08:00","id":1284166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition?p=1284112#post1284112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, the v5 core also gave a werewolf NPC antagonist near the back of the book, which had the same regeneration rules, but no Rage value assigned in that NPC's block, though the NPC had high levels of Disciplines (for ease of using the NPC prior to W5's creation, bless the writer's hearts) to emulate gifts (I recall the V20, W20 and M20 books doing much the same thing), though since Hunger is risked for higher ranked disciplines, I imagine that as of the corebook's writing the Rage mechanic, like Hunger may be risked to perform certain supernatural feats, and if it rises too fill the Lupine to bursting with Rage, that's when things get Crinos rampage messy. The NPC stats also had some shapeshifting mechanics for Crinos form it seems. No sign in either the pre-alpha or the final V5 of Werewolf Gnosis or specific info or hints on how Breeds, Auspices, Gifts or Tribes work, though I imagine, as in times past, the Tribe will be the equivalent of Clan in terms of mechanical and story significance.</div> </div> </div> </div>i think they may have been still considering allowing multiple actions a round during that playtest and by v5 final they decided &quot;nope&quot; though.. if W5 keeps it and v5 doesnt man werewolves will be even more death to Kindred than before..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T04:30:05-08:00","id":1284316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition?p=1284166#post1284166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i think they may have been still considering allowing multiple actions a round during that playtest and by v5 final they decided &quot;nope&quot; though.. if W5 keeps it and v5 doesnt man werewolves will be even more death to Kindred than before..</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. the multiple actions use of Rage appears to be out, which will level the playing field a bit. The Regeneration rules still make them incredibly lethal to everyone though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T06:46:44-08:00","id":1284333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition?p=1284316#post1284316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. the multiple actions use of Rage appears to be out, which will level the playing field a bit. The Regeneration rules still make them incredibly lethal to everyone though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well celerity ALSO no longer has multiple actions. Multiple actions were one of the more universally reviled parts of classic WOD combat. On the otherhand if the V5 pg reintroduces them for &quot;classic&quot; feel I imagine Rage will make the same offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T09:22:03-08:00","id":1284360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition?p=1284333#post1284333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well celerity ALSO no longer has multiple actions. Multiple actions were one of the more universally reviled parts of classic WOD combat. On the otherhand if the V5 pg reintroduces them for &quot;classic&quot; feel I imagine Rage will make the same offer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I imagine multiple actions will remain out of the main rules. Reintroduction, if it happens at all, would perhaps be in players' guides like the one Modiphius is working on for V5 presently, and even then would likely offer them as option should Storytellers and Players both wish it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T20:24:43-08:00","id":1284645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition?p=1284360#post1284360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. I imagine multiple actions will remain out of the main rules. Reintroduction, if it happens at all, would perhaps be in players' guides like the one Modiphius is working on for V5 presently, and even then would likely offer them as option should Storytellers and Players both wish it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its hard to read long term from v5 to other wod games as there seems to be some serious derailment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T03:44:23-08:00","id":1285522,"title":"","content":"Yeah, don't take anything stated about werewolves in the alpha playtests as indicative of how W5 will / may look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T11:09:59-08:00","id":1286232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition?p=1285522#post1285522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, don't take anything stated about werewolves in the alpha playtests as indicative of how W5 will / may look.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, alpha playtests being far cries from final drafts. I'll focus on the V5 core's antagonist entry of Lupine<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T11:15:29-08:00","id":1286237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition?p=1286232#post1286232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point, alpha playtests being far cries from final drafts. I'll focus on the V5 core's antagonist entry of Lupine</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't take that as an indication either. I wrote that entry without any sight of plans for W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T11:16:57-08:00","id":1286239,"title":"","content":"Currently, the news about W5's content is pretty much nothing. Don't be disheartened by that, but I certainly don't think anyone should be reading into werewolf-as-antagonist entries or Vampire alpha tests for clues. There aren't any clues out there yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T18:57:47-08:00","id":1286939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition?p=1286239#post1286239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently, the news about W5's content is pretty much nothing. Don't be disheartened by that, but I certainly don't think anyone should be reading into werewolf-as-antagonist entries or Vampire alpha tests for clues. There aren't any clues out there yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood. Thanks for clearing it up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:17:16-08:00","id":1287696,"title":"","content":"Well, hopefully the lack of W5 in any forseeable future might encourage another look at publishing some more W20 books......a bloke can dream....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T22:24:47-08:00","id":1288171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition?p=1287696#post1287696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, hopefully the lack of W5 in any forseeable future might encourage another look at publishing some more W20 books......a bloke can dream....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I doubt that too.. honestly the only thing it could really use would be a Lore of the tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T05:05:27-08:00","id":1288901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition?p=1284112#post1284112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;This is the weirdest one. If the coterie just sneaks into the wild to walk to a smaller town past the<br /> lockdown and steal a car there, they encounter -something- hunting for them. It\u2019s a Get of Fenris<br /> Lupine from the Grunewald Sept. They can run, but the wolf never loses their scent.<br /> <br /> Lupine Tracker<br /> Mental 2 Physical 5 Social 2<br /> Alertness 2 Combat 5 Other 1<br /> Potence 3 Fortitude 3 Rage 8<br /> Willpower 3 Health 9 Composure 1<br /> <br /> The Lupine tracker can spend Rage to gain extra actions (up to two extra per round) and<br /> regenerates one point of Superficial damage each turn. It does not suffer wound penalties and its<br /> claws and bite deal aggravated damage. Good luck! THE END&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not related to the topic, but can I just say what sweet bullshit that is. Players use their heads and nope out of the city through safer roads, then they get attacked by a -single- garou and it is automatic game over? WoD isn't fair, but that is just railroady.<br /> <br /> To the topic at hand, I personally think Paradox is severly restructuring nuWW before anything official gets published about 5th editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T20:52:19-08:00","id":1289078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1283793-estimated-date-for-5th-edition?p=1288901#post1288901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not related to the topic, but can I just say what sweet bullshit that is. Players use their heads and nope out of the city through safer roads, then they get attacked by a -single- garou and it is automatic game over? WoD isn't fair, but that is just railroady.<br /> <br /> To the topic at hand, I personally think Paradox is severly restructuring nuWW before anything official gets published about 5th editions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Its what my Group calls a T-rex in the Cornfield.. from a DM having pulled that shit.","signature